<mujoco model="cube">
  <!-- A FREE-JOINTED PROP — the thing a family's `free` slot instantiates.

       ⚠ `angle="radian"` MATCHES THE ROBOT ASSETS ON PURPOSE. `expander.mojo`
       RAISES when an attached model's `<compiler angle>` differs from the
       host's, because a text splice would read this file's numbers in the
       host's units — a 90 would become 90 radians. It refuses rather than
       silently reinterpreting, so the fix is to agree, here.

       ⚠ NO `<inertial>`. MuJoCo derives mass and inertia from the geom's
       shape and density when a body declares none, and so does our builder
       (`model/inertia_from_geom.mojo`). Writing our own would be a SECOND
       implementation of that derivation, checkable against MuJoCo only by
       accident. See `studio/scene.mojo`'s Prop for the same rule. -->
  <compiler angle="radian"/>
  <worldbody>
    <body name="cube">
      <freejoint name="free"/>
      <!-- ⚠⚠ 0.012, NOT 0.02 — THE SO-101 JAW CANNOT CLOSE ON A 4 cm CUBE.
           Measured by `examples/tasks/task_grasp_feasibility.mojo`, which
           hands the controller a closed grasp for free and holds the arm
           still: a 0.04 m cube is held at 0 of 250 placements and a 0.03 m
           one at none either, while a 0.024 m cube is held at z 0.267 with
           four gripper contacts, at rest, and still there half a second
           later. The usable opening is between 2.4 and 3 cm.

           `so101_lift_brick` returned 0.0 on two 1M-step runs with textbook
           critics because of this line, not because of its reward.

           ⚠ `family_config.SLOT_RADIUS` MUST MATCH. The sampler uses it for
           BOTH the pairwise clash test and the resting height
           (`z = site_z + radius`), so a prop smaller than the radius spawns
           floating and drops at reset. -->
      <geom name="geom" type="box" size="0.012 0.012 0.012" density="500"
            rgba="0.2 0.6 0.9 1"/>
    </body>
  </worldbody>
</mujoco>
